egistration of a Pair of Images, with A Contrario Elimination of Outliers", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 59, "title": " Exemplar-based Texture Synthesis: the Efros-Leung Algorithm", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 58, "title": "An Implementation and Detailed Analysis of the K-SVD Image Denoising Algorithm", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 56, "title": "Gunturk-Altunbasak-Mersereau Alternating Projections Image Demosaicking", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 55, "title": "Non-Local Means Denoising", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 52, "title": "The Implementation of SURE Guided Piecewise Linear Image Denoising", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 51, "title": "Simplest Color Balance", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 50, "title": " Self-Similarity Driven Demosaicking", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 47, "title": "Study of the Principal Component Analysis Method for the Correction of Images Degraded by Turbulence", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 45, "title": "Analysis and Extension of the Ponomarenko et al Method Estimating a Noise Curve from a Single Image", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 44, "title": "An Implementation of Combined Local-Global Optical Flow", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 43, "title": "Image Color Cube Dimensional Filtering and Visualization", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 41, "title": " Selective Contrast Adjustment by Poisson Equation ", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 38, "title": "LSD: a Line Segment Detector", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 35, "title": " A Review of Classic Edge Detectors", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 30, "title": "Local Color Correction", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 28, "title": "Rudin-Osher-Fatemi Total Variation Denoising using Split Bregman", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 27, "title": " Color and Contrast Enhancement by Controlled Piecewise Affine Histogram Equalization ", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 26, "title": "TV-L1 Optical Flow Estimation", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 25, "title": "DCT image denoising: a simple and effective image denoising algorithm", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 23, "title": "Interpolation of Missing Samples in Audio Signals Based on Autoregressive Modeling", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 22, "title": "An analysis and implementation of the BM3D image denoising method", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 21, "title": "Robust Optical Flow Estimation", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 20, "title": "Horn-Schunck Optical Flow with a Multi-Scale Strategy", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 18, "title": " The Flutter Shutter Camera Simulator", "state": "published"}, {"editorsdemoid": 16, "title": "Implementation of the \"Non-Local Bayes\" (NL-Bayes) Image Denoising Algorithm", "state": "published"}];
        const showInfo = true;

        if (showInfo) {
            document.getElementById('info-container').innerHTML = `
                <div class='info-box'>
                    <p>The demos whose ID begins with <strong>'77777'</strong> are public workshops and those with <strong>'33333'</strong> are private.<br>
                    Example demos begin with <strong>'11111'</strong>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class='info-box warning'>
                    <p><strong>Note:</strong> Test demos begin with <strong>'55555'</strong>. These are intended for brief usage and evaluation, and will be automatically removed after a period of inactivity.</p>
                </div>
            `;
        }

        const container = document.getElementById('demos-container');
        const searchInput = document.getElementById('search-input');

        function renderDemos(filterText = '') {
            container.innerHTML = ''; // Clear container
            const lowerFilter = filterText.toLowerCase();

            // Group by state
            const demosByState = {};
            let matchCount = 0;

            demos.forEach(demo => {
                const searchStr = `${demo.title} ${demo.editorsdemoid} ${demo.state}`.toLowerCase();

                // If there's a filter and it isn't found in the text, skip it
                if (lowerFilter && !searchStr.includes(lowerFilter)) {
                    return;
                }

                if (!demosByState[demo.state]) {
                    demosByState[demo.state] = [];
                }
                demosByState[demo.state].push(demo);
                matchCount++;
            });



            if (matchCount === 0) {
                container.innerHTML = '<div class="no-results">No demos found matching your search.</div>';
                return;
            }

            // Render each state
            let htmlChunks = [];
            Object.keys(demosByState).forEach(state => {
                const stateDemos = demosByState[state];
                // Sort by demo ID descending
                stateDemos.sort((a, b) => {
                    const idA = parseInt(a.editorsdemoid, 10) || 0;
                    const idB = parseInt(b.editorsdemoid, 10) || 0;
                    return idB - idA;
                });

                let groupHtml = `<h2 id="${state}">${state}</h2><div class="demo-group">`;

                stateDemos.forEach(demo => {
                    const demoIdStr = String(demo.editorsdemoid);
                    const isPrivate = demoIdStr.startsWith('33333');
                    const privateBadge = isPrivate ? " <span class='badge private'>(private)</span>" : "";

                    groupHtml += `
                        <a class="demo-item" href="/demo/clientApp/demo.html?id=${demo.editorsdemoid}" target="_blank">
                            <span class="demo-id">Demo #${demo.editorsdemoid}</span>${privateBadge}: 
                            <span class="demo-title">${demo.title}</span>
                        </a>
                    `;
                });

                groupHtml += `</div>`;
                htmlChunks.push(groupHtml);
            });

            container.innerHTML = htmlChunks.join('');
        }

        function initStatsBar() {
            const allByState = {};
            demos.forEach(demo => {
                if (!allByState[demo.state]) allByState[demo.state] = 0;
                allByState[demo.state]++;
            });
            const statsBar = document.getElementById('stats-bar');
            let statsHtml = `<div class="stats-card stats-total"><span class="stats-number">${demos.length}</span><span class="stats-label">total</span></div>`;
            Object.keys(allByState).forEach(state => {
                statsHtml += `<div class="stats-card"><span class="stats-number">${allByState[state]}</span><span class="stats-label">${state}</span></div>`;
            });
            statsBar.innerHTML = statsHtml;
        }

        // Attach event listener for filtering (debounced)
        let searchTimeout;
        searchInput.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
            clearTimeout(searchTimeout);
            searchTimeout = setTimeout(() => {
                renderDemos(e.target.value);
                // Reset focus when typing
                currentFocusIndex = -1;
                updateFocus();
            }, 150);
        });

        // Keyboard navigation state
        let currentFocusIndex = -1;

        function updateFocus() {
            const items = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.demo-item'));
            items.forEach((item, index) => {
                if (index === currentFocusIndex) {
                    item.classList.add('keyboard-focused');
                    // Scroll into view if needed
                    item.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
                } else {
                    item.classList.remove('keyboard-focused');
                }
            });
        }

        // Global hotkey to focus search '/' and handle arrow keys
        document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
            const isInputFocused = document.activeElement.tagName === 'INPUT' || document.activeElement.tagName === 'TEXTAREA';
            const items = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.demo-item'));

            if (e.key === '/') {
                if (isInputFocused) return;
                e.preventDefault();
                searchInput.focus();
                return;
            }

            if (e.key === 'ArrowDown') {
                e.preventDefault();
                if (items.length > 0) {
                    currentFocusIndex = Math.min(currentFocusIndex + 1, items.length - 1);
                    updateFocus();
                    // Blur search to prevent input cursor from moving
                    if (isInputFocused) searchInput.blur();
                }
            } else if (e.key === 'ArrowUp') {
                e.preventDefault();
                if (items.length > 0) {
                    currentFocusIndex = Math.max(currentFocusIndex - 1, -1);
                    if (currentFocusIndex === -1) {
                        // Focus back onto the search input
                        updateFocus();
                        searchInput.focus();
                        // Put cursor at end of input
                        const val = searchInput.value;
                        searchInput.value = '';
                        searchInput.value = val;
                    } else {
                        updateFocus();
                    }
                }
            } else if (e.key === 'Enter') {
                if (currentFocusIndex >= 0 && currentFocusIndex < items.length) {
                    e.preventDefault();
                    items[currentFocusIndex].click();
                }
            } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {
                if (isInputFocused) searchInput.blur();
                searchInput.value = '';
                currentFocusIndex = -1;
                renderDemos();
                updateFocus();
            }
        });

        // Initial render
        initStatsBar();
        renderDemos();
    </script>
</body>

</html>